[{"data":1,"prerenderedAt":2156},["ShallowReactive",2],{"page-\u002Fgo\u002F20-context":3},{"id":4,"title":5,"body":6,"description":2149,"extension":2150,"meta":2151,"navigation":120,"path":2152,"seo":2153,"stem":2154,"__hash__":2155},"content\u002Fgo\u002F20-context.md","20 — Context",{"type":7,"value":8,"toc":2140},"minimark",[9,13,27,32,54,58,497,515,519,526,798,811,815,821,1057,1066,1070,1256,1259,1263,2136],[10,11,5],"h1",{"id":12},"_20-context",[14,15,16,17,21,22,26],"p",{},"The ",[18,19,20],"code",{},"context"," package is Go's mechanism for ",[23,24,25],"strong",{},"cancellation, deadlines, and request-scoped values"," across API boundaries and goroutines. It's the standard way to propagate \"stop\" signals and per-request data.",[28,29,31],"h2",{"id":30},"the-three-responsibilities","The Three Responsibilities",[33,34,35,42,48],"ol",{},[36,37,38,41],"li",{},[23,39,40],{},"Cancellation"," — signal goroutines to stop early (user canceled, parent operation done).",[36,43,44,47],{},[23,45,46],{},"Deadlines"," — a time by which the operation should be cancelled.",[36,49,50,53],{},[23,51,52],{},"Values"," — request-scoped data (request ID, user ID) carried through the call chain.",[28,55,57],{"id":56},"creating-contexts","Creating Contexts",[59,60,62],"code-wrapper",{"language":61},"go",[63,64,68],"pre",{"className":65,"code":66,"language":61,"meta":67,"style":67},"language-go shiki shiki-themes github-light github-dark","ctx := context.Background()   \u002F\u002F the root, never canceled, no deadline\nctx := context.TODO()         \u002F\u002F placeholder when you're not sure which to use\n\nctx, cancel := context.WithCancel(parent)\ndefer cancel()   \u002F\u002F always call cancel to release resources\n\nctx, cancel := context.WithTimeout(parent, 5*time.Second)\ndefer cancel()\n\nctx, cancel := context.WithDeadline(parent, time.Now().Add(5*time.Second))\ndefer cancel()\n\nctx = context.WithValue(parent, \"requestID\", \"abc123\")\n``\n::\n\nEvery context is derived from a **parent** — they form a tree. Canceling a parent cancels all its children.\n\n### The `cancel` function\n\n`WithCancel`\u002F`WithTimeout`\u002F`WithDeadline` return a context and a `cancel` function. **Always call `cancel`** (typically `defer cancel()`) to release resources (timers, goroutines) — even if the operation completes normally. Forgetting `cancel` leaks.\n\n## Checking for Cancellation\n\n::code-wrapper{language=\"go\"}\n```go\nselect {\ncase \u003C-ctx.Done():\n    return ctx.Err()   \u002F\u002F context.Canceled or context.DeadlineExceeded\ndefault:\n    \u002F\u002F continue\n}\n\n\u002F\u002F Or in a blocking wait\n\u003C-ctx.Done()\nerr := ctx.Err()   \u002F\u002F why it was canceled\n``\n","",[18,69,70,97,115,122,138,152,157,182,192,197,231,240,245,273,279,285,290,307,312,324,329,386,391,403,408,428,434,440,446,452,458,464,469,474,480,486,492],{"__ignoreMap":67},[71,72,75,79,83,86,90,93],"span",{"class":73,"line":74},"line",1,[71,76,78],{"class":77},"ssxIu","ctx ",[71,80,82],{"class":81},"svdQ7",":=",[71,84,85],{"class":77}," context.",[71,87,89],{"class":88},"sIsaT","Background",[71,91,92],{"class":77},"()   ",[71,94,96],{"class":95},"sdCPZ","\u002F\u002F the root, never canceled, no deadline\n",[71,98,100,102,104,106,109,112],{"class":73,"line":99},2,[71,101,78],{"class":77},[71,103,82],{"class":81},[71,105,85],{"class":77},[71,107,108],{"class":88},"TODO",[71,110,111],{"class":77},"()         ",[71,113,114],{"class":95},"\u002F\u002F placeholder when you're not sure which to use\n",[71,116,118],{"class":73,"line":117},3,[71,119,121],{"emptyLinePlaceholder":120},true,"\n",[71,123,125,128,130,132,135],{"class":73,"line":124},4,[71,126,127],{"class":77},"ctx, cancel ",[71,129,82],{"class":81},[71,131,85],{"class":77},[71,133,134],{"class":88},"WithCancel",[71,136,137],{"class":77},"(parent)\n",[71,139,141,144,147,149],{"class":73,"line":140},5,[71,142,143],{"class":81},"defer",[71,145,146],{"class":88}," cancel",[71,148,92],{"class":77}